  "bridge_contracts": [
    "BC96F4/F8/FC/9700 are four actual contiguousDWORDs: directionbits, signedlength, signedavailable, stepbits. Headerasserts16-byte state and offsets0/4/8/12. Available<=0 or length<=1 writes wholeDWORDlength0 and returns before normalization/map/routing. Only mode==1 adds the length<5 rejection.",
    "The starttile is wrappedDWORDgeometry.grid_start(BCA2D8)+y*228+x. Geometry width/height/origin/border are the actual16-byte BCA2D0..DC layout. Orientation is wholeDwordBCA2E0, through the real routing map_orientation pointer.",
    "Direction subtracts orientation in32bits, immediately stores that wrappedDWORD, then adds8 and stores again only if the wrapped result signbit is set. There is no repeated wrapping/modulo8. Volatile state retains both stores on the negative path.",
    "For mode==1, cached initialcount9/10=>middle4,11/12=>5,13/14=>6,15/16=>7,all others=>8. Every other nonzero mode uses ship pieces but leavesmiddle0 and bypasses the mode1-only length>=5 guard.",
    "StepBC9700 is a cachedDWORD index delta, loaded once. Native bytepointer advances bystep andterrain pointer bystep*4; typed unsignedtile arithmetic preserves32bit wrap/negative-offset encoding and step0 repeated writes. Count is cached and positive by the earlier signedguards.",
    "Each visitedtile first performs a wholeDWORDterrainOR40 atAF598C. ADC36C is a BYTEpiece/direction grid, proven by LEA(tile+ADC36C), BYTEstores and unscaledstep. RawUnit01163 DataUndefined4 pointer units are not used as authority.",
    "Only normalized directions0/2/4/6 write recognizedpiece bytes. Low-first=[4,1,6,3],low-last=[6,3,4,1],low-inner=[5,2,5,2] in direction0/2/4/6 order; last test precedes first. Unsupported directions preserve that byte without a redundant store.",
    "Nonzero-mode glyph priority is index==count-2 thenindex==1 =>BYTE13 regardless of direction; thenlast,first,middle,inside. Ship-first=[7,8,9,10],last=[9,10,7,8],middle=[14,15,14,15],inside=[11,12,11,12]. With nonzero mode!=1,count2 bothcells become13 because those marker tests precede endpoint tests.",
    "After the completeplacementloop execute actual water5178B0, citizen517370 and noncitizen517660 in that exact order. No routed result snapshot, adapter intoOriginal/IL, or substitute callback exists.",
    "Routing operates on the same terrain/piece backing arrays. The real citizen child can subsequently clear bridge-road40 when flags&10044==44 and pieceBYTE0; finalterrain must not be assumedOR40 unconditionally for unsupported-byte cases.",
    "Active ferry records in the citizen rebuild require genuine update_ferry_tiles/detach_ferry providers. Existing pharaoh_ferry_bind_scene_routing in map/ferry_routing.c supplies the real algorithms with an actual fully-backed PharaohFerryContext; the new bridge owner neither invents nor replaces them."
